{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/839919-grimm-seeming-released-first","id":839919,"title":"Grimm Seeming released first","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-01T08:22:43-08:00","id":839919,"title":"Grimm Seeming released first","content":"I was l looking at the schedule and I noticed something ironic. Dark Eras will be released before Changeling 2e, which means that the Grimm Seeming will actually be the first Seeming officially released (previews don't count officially released, they're not the finial verison), not the traditional Seemings of Darkling, Wizened, Fairest, Ogre, and Beasts (and the new Seeming of Loyalist).<br /> <br /> Its just kind of a funny twist of fate to me. I'm looking forward to seeing the Grimm.<br /> <br /> We know Grimms are Changelings who have escaped by playing the roles the Gentry gave them and using said roles against the Gentry some how.<br /> <br /> Any one care to speculate as to what the Grimms Seeming Blessing and Curse will be?<br /> <br /> My guess is that the Blessing is they gain clarity when they act congruantly with their Kith (or Kiths), and maybe they benifit from a couple of free dots or equivilant to Potent Kith Merit, and the Curse would be when they play against type (Kith), its a breaking point and penalty to strengthing the mask, it costs 3 glamour instead of 1. Just a guess.<br /> <br /> Of course I'm curious about the Loyalist Seeming too, so I'll guess that Loyalists blessing is gaining Clarity for service to their Keeper, they get a boost to subtlefudge rolls to blend in, and for a curse disobeying or betraying their Keeper is a breaking point, and have a fewer doors when dealing with the Gentry and their servants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T09:22:49-08:00","id":839965,"title":"","content":"I wonder how they'll incorporate Seeming bonuses for Contracts. Like, will they include a list of new effects for old Contracts or what?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T09:28:59-08:00","id":839970,"title":"","content":"I wager Loyalists and Grimms don't have their own Seeming bonuses.<br /> <br /> Grimms might be able to craft their own Seeming bonuses (which would make them very popular) or choose one of the current Seeming bonuses for free when they purchase the contract, or simply not get any contract bonuses but instead be compensated in a different way.<br /> <br /> I think Loyalists will get some sort of &quot;Seeming-change&quot; mechanic, so they'll be able to infiltrate Freeholds. That means they might get the Seeming bonus of whatever Seeming they're duplicating.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T10:03:42-08:00","id":839992,"title":"","content":"Maybe for Grimms a universal Seeming effect on all Contracts like +1 to all contract activation rolls, which can be bought for one experience point individually for each contract like any other Seeming effect.<br /> <br /> Loyalists will be in the Core Book so they might get Seeming Effects on contracts or they might gain a more Gentry like benifit. Or they might just pick one other Seeming to mimic and get their Seeming Effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T03:10:01-08:00","id":840519,"title":"","content":"It's a really good question. I could see them printing a list of new Seeming bonuses for the new Contracts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/822-daemonchrno","name":"DaemonChrno","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar822_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T06:05:43-08:00","id":840587,"title":"","content":"Is there going to be new contracts for Dark Eras?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T06:55:54-08:00","id":840616,"title":"","content":"Well, there was the blade contracts thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/822-daemonchrno","name":"DaemonChrno","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar822_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T09:02:51-08:00","id":840697,"title":"","content":"Blade contracts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T09:36:08-08:00","id":840716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/839919-grimm-seeming-released-first?p=840697#post840697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Blade contracts?</div> </div> </div> </div> In the French Changeling Dark Age, there was a Contract of the Blade written up in 1E rules. Not sure if they're planing to update it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T23:16:49-08:00","id":841157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/839919-grimm-seeming-released-first?p=840716#post840716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> In the French Changeling Dark Age, there was a Contract of the Blade written up in 1E rules. Not sure if they're planing to update it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I kinda did a stopgap conversion of Saber Dance <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/833785-contracts-2e-conversions#post833785\">right here</a>. Thinking of doing the same for the other clauses, though a few might get folded with one another.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T16:56:39-07:00","id":855343,"title":"","content":"Bump, since the Grimm is out for Kickstarter back (of which I'm not).<br /> <br /> For those who are, how is it? And how does it deal with Contracts and Seeming effects?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T17:19:04-07:00","id":855361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/839919-grimm-seeming-released-first?p=855343#post855343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bump, since the Grimm is out for Kickstarter back (of which I'm not).<br /> <br /> For those who are, how is it? And how does it deal with Contracts and Seeming effects?</div> </div> </div> </div>Seeing as I didn't back it either, I'm interested in knowing too.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T17:25:18-07:00","id":855371,"title":"","content":"Tell you what-I was going to go through this in an orderly, chronological fashion, reading up on all the new stuff, but you guys?<br /> <br /> I like you guys. So I'll go look up the Grimm and give the skinny.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T17:46:16-07:00","id":855386,"title":"","content":"So, the Grimm. I dunno how much of this is era-specific or not, but for the most part, Grimms believe that the recording of stories causes the Hedge to flourish and act as a better wall between Arcadia and the Hedge, and that other acts of cementing the beats and flow of stories certainly help. So they are both the play actors and the record keepers, those who previously found little magic in their lives and now embrace every bit of it as a way to make it 'solid'. They are the people who escape Arcadia by following the path laid out by the Hedge, a promise to bring the stories to the world, to be the stories for the world. They regain Clarity when they get someone to acknowledge them as their role without prompting, and they lose it when they do something beneficial for themselves but out of character. Also, they are noticeable as hell outside of a role. That's the nutshell.<br /> <br /> While it might be superbly easy to label the Seeming as the TvTropers Seeming(In fact, a sidebar sort of rib nudges the notion), there's some good conflict along the lines of the Fairest or the Darklings in the power and danger of expectation. It seems pretty legit. Also, it's icon is badass.<br /> <br /> I have no idea how it works in context. There's probably more hidden awesome in there, but I wanna get back to the Vikings I was hanging out with.<br /> <br /> By the way, Three Kingdoms Changeling is <i>awesome</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T18:00:55-07:00","id":855394,"title":"","content":"Thanks, Arc, you sold me on the book as soon as its available for purpuse by the general public.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T20:11:28-07:00","id":855456,"title":"","content":"I really hope y'all like the Contracts I wrote.<br /> <br /> (Maybe tagging myself here is a mistake, hopefully not?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T20:19:19-07:00","id":855459,"title":"","content":"You also got to see me go full historian here, I hope y'all enjoyed that too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T03:05:09-07:00","id":855599,"title":"","content":"Well, just read it, and I've mixed feelings about the changeling sections of the book. It's great and fun, but the mix between the first and second editions made me always ponder for which version of the game each mechanics were intended. It's just plainly confusing and it's especially apparent in the Grimm section where the new Courts and Seeming are clearly second edition, the new Tokens first edition (for what I know) and the Contracts write up seems all misplaced between first (no Seeming bonus and all the dicepool lacking a Skill) and second (the existence of Conditions) edition while also lacking the exceptional success part. Also, some of these contracts are really overpowered for level one contracts.<br /> <br /> About the Grimm themselves, I really love them even if it seems that something is lacking: their Blessing and Curse lacks the non-Clarity stuffs that other Seemings were previewed to have in the second edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/822-daemonchrno","name":"DaemonChrno","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar822_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T03:33:08-07:00","id":855601,"title":"","content":"Just to address the parts I played a role in.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DaemonChrno</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/839919-grimm-seeming-released-first?p=855599#post855599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Contracts write up seems all misplaced between first (no Seeming bonus and all the dicepool lacking a Skill) and second (the existence of Conditions) edition while also lacking the exceptional success part. Also, some of these contracts are really overpowered for level one contracts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I already brought this up in the Errata to be fixed--long story short, the contracts are not meant to be one dot, and something must have gone wrong after I submitted my final. I just checked my final manuscript again, and the dot values are definitely correct there.<br /> <br /> I wrote the Inspirational Media section, What Has Come Before, the Contracts, and the Companions of the Resigned.<br /> <br /> Also--I don't want you to think I'm ignoring points you brought up--we were given specific instructions re: the edition issue. This was my first contract with the company, and I'm not sure how much I can say on that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":3093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","user":"hm8453a","date":".  Fixed a grammar issue. 03-30-2016, 06:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T04:22:41-07:00","id":855615,"title":"","content":"Here are the correct dot values for the Contracts:<br /> <br /> Contract of Provisional Aid 1<br /> Contract of Real and False Self 1<br /> Contract of Heartwarming Comfort 2<br /> Contract of Transference 3<br /> Contract of Objective Idealism 4<br /> Contract of the Good 5","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":3093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","user":"hm8453a","date":".  Fixed spacing 03-30-2016, 07:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T04:45:42-07:00","id":855617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/839919-grimm-seeming-released-first?p=855615#post855615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here are the correct dot values for the Contracts:<br /> <br /> Contract of Provisional Aid 1<br /> Contract of Real and False Self 1<br /> Contract of Heartwarming Comfort 2<br /> Contract of Transference 3<br /> Contract of Objective Idealism 4<br /> Contract of the Good 5</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, it's much appreciated. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/822-daemonchrno","name":"DaemonChrno","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar822_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T04:48:08-07:00","id":855618,"title":"","content":"Of course!<br /> <br /> As I said, this was my first job with the company, so I'd love constructive crit on what y'all enjoyed and didn't that I had a part in. I'm, personally, in love with the Contracts I wrote and the Entitlement. I went into it wanting to do something with comfort objects and imaginary friends, and there it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T05:45:40-07:00","id":855637,"title":"","content":"I'm one of the regretful sods who didn't back the kickstarter, so I can't check this, but what do the mien of grimm generally LOOK like? Like how fairest are attractive and regal, darklings are shadowy and wizened have some augmentations or replaced body-parts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T07:00:26-07:00","id":855666,"title":"","content":"I think they should have split the Dark Eras into a Dark Eras 1e for the Mummy, Giest, and a 2e Dark Eras for everything else, because none of this actual sounds usable honestly. <br /> <br /> I could see having one era 1e and another era 2e but a single era blending mechanics can't work.<br /> <br /> You can't just intermix incompatible mechanics together and expect something usable. I feel bad for pointing this out, but its not the writers fault, its the person in change.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T07:25:41-07:00","id":855685,"title":"","content":"I do appreciate that the Contracts in the Grimm section are easy to translate back to 1e, though I am curious why none of them have an Exceptional Success effect or Seeming benefit. Also, it seems like there's more mechanics in the &quot;this is what the contract does&quot; section than the &quot;Success&quot; section; I personally prefer mechanics under Success. (There's a part of me that wants these Contracts to work on any mortal, rather than just children, but I understand that doesn't work as well thematically.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DaemonChrno</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/839919-grimm-seeming-released-first?p=855599#post855599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About the Grimm themselves, I really love them even if it seems that something is lacking: their Blessing and Curse lacks the non-Clarity stuffs that other Seemings were previewed to have in the second edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, they do have a non-Clarity curse: they anti-rote rolls to escape Huntsmen/Gentry when not in a role (roll successful dice twice, they only count if they succeed both times). No blessing, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fumus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/839919-grimm-seeming-released-first?p=855637#post855637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm one of the regretful sods who didn't back the kickstarter, so I can't check this, but what do the mien of grimm generally LOOK like? Like how fairest are attractive and regal, darklings are shadowy and wizened have some augmentations or replaced body-parts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Grimm miens reflect whatever &quot;role&quot; they're playing (and there's not really any fluff or mechanics about how these role choices/switches happen, or what a valid &quot;role&quot; is, at least in the Grimm Seeming section). When they're between roles, they seem to become books/words incarnate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T11:42:08-07:00","id":855844,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I thought it was said that the Seemings were going to get a Blessing in addition to their proprietary Clarity trick?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T12:11:30-07:00","id":855872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/839919-grimm-seeming-released-first?p=855844#post855844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I thought it was said that the Seemings were going to get a Blessing in addition to their proprietary Clarity trick?</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember reading that, yeah. I can imagine Grimms getting something like +1 to a Skill that is relevant for the role they're enacting while they're enacting it. Buuuuuuuut I still can't find anything about <i>how </i>the role thing works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T12:15:23-07:00","id":855875,"title":"","content":"I didn't really understand the seeming at a skim, which was sufficient for the others. Will have to give it another try later but it seems a bit opaque","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","name":"Nicias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T12:32:42-07:00","id":855887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/839919-grimm-seeming-released-first?p=855875#post855875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't really understand the seeming at a skim, which was sufficient for the others. Will have to give it another try later but it seems a bit opaque</div> </div> </div> </div>They're people who escaped by playing the Keeper's game. So now those narrative roles are their armor. They fill narrative trope niches as it provides them with identity.<br /> <br /> As we are often talking about the roles their Keeper's give them, they do tend to lean into their Kith, which may be why they're less recognized as a distinct Seeming compared with the core six.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T12:50:13-07:00","id":855904,"title":"","content":"I am liking the idea of the Grimm even more after reading this thread. Really need to catch up with what we know on changeling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Currently Playing:</b> <i>A large, mixed splat game of <b>CofD</b>.</i> <b>As:</b> Seraph du Salomon, Voice on the concordance. Unsubtle man reluctantly participating in the business of Magi. Awakening 2E homebrew <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1338514-house-du-salomon-a-proximus-dynasty?_=1569864567692\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...=1569864567692</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2598-gryphon-s-feather","name":"Gryphon's Feather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2598_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"215"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T15:52:02-07:00","id":856047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/839919-grimm-seeming-released-first?p=855666#post855666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think they should have split the Dark Eras into a Dark Eras 1e for the Mummy, Geist, and a 2e Dark Eras for everything else, because none of this actual sounds usable honestly.<br /> <br /> I could see having one era 1e and another era 2e but a single era blending mechanics can't work.<br /> <br /> You can't just intermix incompatible mechanics together and expect something usable. I feel bad for pointing this out, but its not the writers fault, its the person in change.</div> </div> </div> </div>I second this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/822-daemonchrno","name":"DaemonChrno","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar822_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T16:08:58-07:00","id":856058,"title":"","content":"I know you said it's not my fault, and I appreciate that, but even so, I apologize.<br /> <br /> I hope you enjoy and find use for the Inspirational Media and What Has Come Before, including the Story Hooks I wrote, even if you have trouble finding ways to incorporate the mechanics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T16:39:56-07:00","id":856072,"title":"","content":"I enjoy the book and the part you cited, and I can't complain about all the ideas and stuffs that were added into it: this book will provide me with inspirations for my games for years to come, and it's already really good for that. And it's only while having just read the changelings sections of the book. It's wonderful.<br /> <br /> The only problem that I have is to know that I will have to house rule a supplement even before having it into my hands. I mean, there was a big expectation about this, but it will be the only official thing that we will have for a very long time regarding some of the mechanics (if not the only one for the Grimm seeming and some of the Courts), and it's bugged and not adapted for what it was mean to be. It's just feel like someone pushed the mechanics for the second edition without having them already fixed, and it's feel like a wasted effort since it's already unusable and out-of-date for what we know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/822-daemonchrno","name":"DaemonChrno","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar822_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T17:44:30-07:00","id":856104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DaemonChrno</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/839919-grimm-seeming-released-first?p=856072#post856072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I enjoy the book and the part you cited, and I can't complain about all the ideas and stuffs that were added into it: this book will provide me with inspirations for my games for years to come, and it's already really good for that. And it's only while having just read the changelings sections of the book. It's wonderful.<br /> <br /> The only problem that I have is to know that I will have to house rule a supplement even before having it into my hands. I mean, there was a big expectation about this, but it will be the only official thing that we will have for a very long time regarding some of the mechanics (if not the only one for the Grimm seeming and some of the Courts), and it's bugged and not adapted for what it was mean to be. It's just feel like someone pushed the mechanics for the second edition without having them already fixed, and it's feel like a wasted effort since it's already unusable and out-of-date for what we know.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand your frustrations. Until recently, I was just a fan myself. I've made a promise to myself to try and be here, because I want to interact with readers, I want to share excitement at receiving new texts with you, and I want to learn how to improve. Maybe the writers who wrote the Seeming and the Courts will come here to lend a hand to the houseruling. I know a lot of us try to be here. I'm not the only one, I'm not even close. I wish I had more of an answer or more of a way to help. I feel like I'm going in circles with this, but your feelings are valid. I'll leave it at that. I understand where you're coming from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T21:27:53-07:00","id":856233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/839919-grimm-seeming-released-first?p=855618#post855618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course!<br /> <br /> As I said, this was my first job with the company, so I'd love constructive crit on what y'all enjoyed and didn't that I had a part in. I'm, personally, in love with the Contracts I wrote and the Entitlement. I went into it wanting to do something with comfort objects and imaginary friends, and there it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>You should definitely be in love with that Entitlement! I have contemplated playing an imaginary friend character on several occasions, and this Entitlement would be perfect for that. I feel no reservation whatsoever in giving you what I think may be the greatest compliment possible for such a thing: I want to play one of these.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/839919-grimm-seeming-released-first?p=855872#post855872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I remember reading that, yeah. I can imagine Grimms getting something like +1 to a Skill that is relevant for the role they're enacting while they're enacting it. Buuuuuuuut I still can't find anything about <i>how </i>the role thing works.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the houserule I'm going to use for it until we get something more official is to make their blessing the opposite of their curse. In my games, while playing their roles, they'll have the rote quality to elude the Fae and Huntsmen. As for how the roles work, I'll have to agree that the text doesn't make it very clear. I can understand the effects of when they are in a role and out of one, but not how one goes about choosing and switching roles, or why one would ever be without one. It also mentions that other changelings can tell that the character is the Grimm even when they're in a role, but that they'll perceive their mien as the role they've taken on. It makes me wonder whether it is something that they can recognize visually or if it is simply a matter of understanding that it is the same individual on an intuitive level. I also wonder how much the Grimm's kith is visible when they are in a role. If a Fireheart takes on the role of Cinderella, do they still seem like a Fireheart, or would new changelings meeting them assume that they were a Drudge?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T05:13:06-07:00","id":856393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/839919-grimm-seeming-released-first?p=856058#post856058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know you said it's not my fault, and I appreciate that, but even so, I apologize.<br /> <br /> I hope you enjoy and find use for the Inspirational Media and What Has Come Before, including the Story Hooks I wrote, even if you have trouble finding ways to incorporate the mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div>You never blame the soldier, you blame the General.<br /> <br /> I'm sure the What has Come Before and Inspirational Media will be fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 03-31-2016, 08:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T05:22:19-07:00","id":856400,"title":"","content":"&quot;It's just feel like someone pushed the mechanics for the second edition without having them already fixed.&quot;<br /> <br /> Exactly, now I'm questioning if I want to buy this for broken mechanics. I mean I can deal with that some chapters are 1e, but the ones that are 2e should at least use updated mechanics.<br /> <br /> If Grimm for example only has a blessing and curse that only effects clarity, then playing it, will be a major disadvantage compared others Seemings that can see in the dark or ignore wound penalties.<br /> <br /> And if the dice pools of contracts are gimped by lacking adding a skill to them, people are unlikely to pick them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T23:00:48-07:00","id":858175,"title":"","content":"Frankly, crunch is easy to fix, and I wouldn't be surprised if we see a whole bunch of <i>Dark Eras</i> errata come out down the line as the 2e rules are actually published. If you want to use the mechanics now, just add some traits to the dice pools that make sense, and come up with some blessing and curse effects that make sense (we should probably make a thread for that).<br /> <br /> The concepts are more interesting than the mechanics anyway; I consider the book well worth the price.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3209,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","user":"CatDoom","date":". 04-03-2016, 02:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T23:11:16-07:00","id":858179,"title":"","content":"The mechanics are flawed, but no so badly they're inusable(In fact, they are quite usable), and they maintain a lot of interest as story catalysts or twists.<br /> <br /> And the rest of this chapter is <i>gold</i>. Easily among the best eras in the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 04-03-2016, 02:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}